    "summary": "Epic Dark Star → Saint Stephen chain with soaring Turn On Your Lovelight",
    "blurb": "The second set erupts with a monumental Dark Star that morphs into Saint Stephen and rolls straight into a thunderous Not Fade Away. Jerry’s tone is immaculate, while the rhythm section drives an ecstatic Turn On Your Lovelight finale. The show is consistently praised for its tight flow and high‑energy improvisations.",
    "review": "On September 19, 1970 at the Fillmore East the Grateful Dead delivered one of their most memorable early‑’70 outings. After a solid first set of folk‑rock staples, the second set kicked off with a Dark Star that many reviewers call “out‑of‑this‑world” and “angelic,” showcasing Jerry Garcia’s flawless tone, daring wah‑pedal explorations, and an improvisational stretch that seamlessly segues into Saint Stephen. The momentum never wanes: Not Fade Away bursts forth with a ferocious China Cat tease before the band launches into a joyous Turn On Your Lovelight, Pigpen’s harmonica soaring over Mickey Hart’s “cannon” fills and Bill Kreutzmann’s propulsive drumming. Highlights like Morning Dew and Easy Wind add depth, but it’s the second‑set cascade that cements this night as a must‑listen classic.",
